# Design: Organize documentation with Diátaxis

## Problem
The v0.3 documentation mixed tutorials, task procedures, contract lookup, and design rationale on the same topic pages, making navigation and maintenance harder.

## Approach
Organize the sidebar by Tutorials, How-to, Reference, and Explanation. Split mixed program, history, recovery, model-selection, and shell-integration content into focused pages while retaining the old paths as navigation maps. Add metadata and a CI drift checker for classification, links, release versions, CLI coverage, provider language, and qualification status.

## Key Trade-offs
- More focused pages and files, with stable topic maps preserving old URLs.
- Some facts are linked to canonical references rather than repeated in procedural pages.
- Crate packaging now includes the complete Markdown hierarchy.

## Verification
Formatting, docs drift checks, strict Clippy, all 390 Rust tests, and crate packaging passed.
